Andrew,
Allow me to add my congratulations. The work does pay off.

I'll go ahead and recommend Robin Powell's la nicte cadzu, an original novel
in progress. I read the then-finished sections some time ago and found it to
be not-difficult, although admittedly I think I had finished CLL by that
point. First four chapters are complete according to this page, which I'm
taking as current: <
http://www.digitalkingdom.org/~rlpowell/hobbies/lojban/palm/la%20nicte%20cadzu/index.html>
. I'm sure Robin will correct me if I'm wrong.

Enjoy your wanderings through the bubbling swamps of Jbogug.

mu'o mi'e komfo,amonan

